Language Technology Development Index (LTDI)
https://github.com/sandyfritchie/ltdi

Code: MIT licence (LICENSE).

Data: the data the Index publishes (data/, the scores, and the site's data files under site/) is
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/. Attribute it as "Language Technology Development
Index (langtechindex.org)", and keep the attributions below for the upstream data it draws on.

Each upstream source keeps its own terms. The ones whose data the Index redistributes or derives
values from, as each source states them:

- LinguaMeta (Google Research): compiled from sources with their own licences, listed in its README:
  Google Research CC BY 4.0, Glottolog CC BY 4.0, IETF CC BY 4.0, Unicode CLDR (Unicode licence),
  SIL ISO 639 code tables (SIL's terms of use), Wikidata (CC0 / CC BY-SA 3.0), Wikipedia and
  Wiktionary (CC BY-SA 4.0).
  https://github.com/google-research/url-nlp/tree/main/linguameta
- QQ (qwanqwa; Poelman, Chen & de Lhoneux): data CC BY-SA 4.0, software Apache 2.0. Data derived
  from QQ is why the Index's data is CC BY-SA 4.0. https://github.com/WPoelman/qwanqwa
- Glottolog: CC BY 4.0. https://glottolog.org
- Glottography, Asher & Moseley's Atlas of the World's Languages (contemporary version) and
  Wikipedia's official languages by country: CC BY 4.0. https://glottography.github.io
- Unicode CLDR: Unicode License v3. https://www.unicode.org/license.txt
- Lingua Libre recordings (Wikimedia Commons): CC BY-SA 4.0; each clip credits its speaker on the
  language's page. https://lingualibre.org
- UDHR in XML (Eric Muller), from the translations collected by the UN Office of the High
  Commissioner for Human Rights: the project states no licence; Article 1 is quoted with a link to
  each file. https://github.com/eric-muller/udhr
- FineWeb-2 (Hugging Face): Open Data Commons Attribution (ODC-By); only word counts and character
  samples are used. https://huggingface.co/datasets/HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2
- World Bank World Development Indicators: CC BY 4.0, with the World Bank's additional terms.
  https://data.worldbank.org/summary-terms-of-use
- UNdata (UN Statistics Division) census tables: "may be copied freely, duplicated and further
  distributed provided that UNdata is cited as the reference." https://data.un.org
- US Census Bureau, American Community Survey: a work of the US government.
  https://www.census.gov
- Natural Earth (via world-atlas, ISC licence): public domain. https://www.naturalearthdata.com
- Wikipedia statistics and infobox speaker counts: CC BY-SA 4.0. https://meta.wikimedia.org
- OPUS, Universal Dependencies, Hugging Face Hub datasets, open speech datasets and benchmarks:
  only counts are recorded (sentence pairs, words, hours, datasets, results); each corpus, treebank
  or dataset keeps its own licence, given on its own page.
- Company and provider language lists: facts read from public documentation (which languages a
  product supports); each value links to the page it came from. No affiliation with, or endorsement
  by, any company is implied.
